   plugins/databricks/LICENSE). Not derived from upstream content.

Per-file mapping (upstream path -> local path):

  skills/databricks-core/SKILL.md
    -> plugins/databricks/skills/databricks-core/SKILL.md
  skills/databricks-core/databricks-cli-auth.md
    -> plugins/databricks/skills/databricks-core/databricks-cli-auth.md
  skills/databricks-core/data-exploration.md
    -> plugins/databricks/skills/databricks-core/data-exploration.md

NOT ported from this upstream skill: skills/databricks-core/databricks-cli-install.md.
CLI installation is the user's responsibility; the upstream's 100+ line install
walkthrough was out of scope for an agent skill that assumes the CLI is on PATH.
The SKILL.md Prerequisites section was simplified to a one-line "must be installed"
check, and the install-related cross-references in the "Required Reading" and
"Reference Guides" tables were removed in the same port-time pass.

Mechanical edits applied at port time (databricks-core only):

  - Em-dash sentence-pause: U+0020 U+2014 U+0020 -> U+002C U+0020 ("comma + space").
  - Em-dash labelled-bullet: <bold> U+2014 U+0020 -> U+003A U+0020 ("colon + space").
  - En-dash numeric-range: <digit> U+2013 <digit> -> "-" (hyphen).
  - Em-dash heading-internal: substituted with U+003A U+0020 ("colon + space").
  - Em-dash code-block-internal: substituted with U+003A U+0020 ("colon + space").
  - Frontmatter: dropped "metadata.version: 0.1.0" (collides with plugin
    version). Kept "name", "description", "compatibility".
  - Body: removed the upstream "Product Skills" section listing the six
    unported dependent skills (databricks-jobs, databricks-pipelines,
    databricks-apps, databricks-lakebase, databricks-model-serving).
  - Layout: kept the upstream's flat sibling layout for the three reference
    files so the nine internal markdown links continue to resolve without
    rewriting.
  - Dropped: upstream skills/databricks-core/agents/ (Codex marketplace v2
    plumbing) and skills/databricks-core/assets/ (referenced only by the
    dropped agents/ file).

Later local edits (databricks-core SKILL.md):

  - "Profile Selection": replaced the rule never to auto-select a profile
    with named exceptions (a profile the user named or chose, a single
    profile), and added which commands run without asking.

NOT ported from upstream (out of scope for this PR): databricks-apps,
databricks-dabs, databricks-jobs, databricks-lakebase,
databricks-model-serving, databricks-pipelines,
databricks-serverless-migration. The databricks-docs skill replaces them
with live docs.databricks.com lookups.
